    "rules": [
      "Retrieve incident reporting only; do not retrieve production instructions.",
      "Require a reported non-state terrorism nexus; exclude accidents, routine industry, exercises and ordinary crime.",
      "Keep firearms and generic weapons reporting in its existing category.",
      "Terms describing instructions, manufacturing, procurement, components or dispersal may only identify news or official reports of a concrete investigation, seizure, prosecution, plot or terrorist incident. Reject manuals, recipes, technical procedures, vendor listings and instructional source documents; do not reproduce their contents or link to them.",
      "Names of substances, precursors, schedules or circuits are not sufficient for classification. Require the material to be central to the reported incident and preserve alleged, suspected, threat and hoax status.",
      "For mixed incidents use one canonical event record. Apply a biological or radiological label only when separately supported by the reporting. A CBRN-enhanced explosive reference does not create a CBRN parent category."
